Author:     Glen Taggart <glenmtaggart@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Sun May 17 14:23:45 2026 -0700
Commit:     Glen Taggart <glenmtaggart@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun May 17 14:23:45 2026 -0700

    point the slotted-instance error at the decorator API
    
    The (very good) error message predated the decorators and didn't mention
    class_swap. Rewrote it to direct users to
    paramsight.slotted_strategies: @add_field (real field; note it must sit
    *below* @define/@dataclass), @uses_class_swap (synthetic swap; no field
    pollution; type-identity trade-off), @uses_side_table (out-of-band; no
    pickle survival; weakref-able), with the class-body marker noted as
    equivalent for the strategy ones, and the class-side-only escape. Still
    contains __orig_class__ / _paramsight_slots so existing pytest match=
    patterns hold.
    
    ruff clean, pyright (src) 0/0/0, pytest 136.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

